% ============================================================================
% karst-process-zone.query.adj — worked recall over the karst-process-zone
% library.
% ============================================================================
% The shape a learner (or an LLM) produces to ANSWER "where can speleothems
% actually form?" (direct), "which process happens in the zone of
% aeration?" (reverse), or "do caves always form below the water table?"
% (abstain — the source says TYPICALLY, and the hedge lives in the atom, so
% a query for the unhedged zone correctly finds nothing) — it states no
% fact of its own — it only `import`s the grounded table and asks binding
% queries.
%
% Run (from this directory so the relative import resolves):
%     ../../../../packages/rust/target/debug/adj-lang-cli karst-process-zone.query.adj
% ============================================================================

import "karst-process-zone.adj"

? karst_process_zone(speleothem_deposition, $Z)      % expect zone_of_aeration -- deposition "is not possible until" caves are above the water table
? karst_process_zone(cave_formation, $Z)             % expect zone_of_saturation_typically -- the hedge rides in the atom, not dropped
? karst_process_zone($P, zone_of_aeration)           % expect speleothem_deposition (reverse)
? karst_process_zone($P, zone_of_saturation)         % expect abstain -- the UNHEDGED zone is not a value here; the source says caves form there TYPICALLY, never always
? karst_process_zone(dissolution, $Z)                % expect abstain -- a real karst process this source never places relative to the water table
